        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_1",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Does insurance cover this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_1",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Zavelyn is usually a self-pay device — but some private insurers may cover it after individual review.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_2",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Why was it created?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_2",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Zavelyn was developed to solve a major problem: Most patients stop progressing once therapy sessions end. You need guided movement every day — not once a week. Zavelyn brings clinic-level hand therapy into the home.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_3",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "How long does it last?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_3",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>With normal daily use, Zavelyn is built to last years. The tension system, control module, and tubing are designed for repeated cycles and long-term rehabilitation routines.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_4",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Will it help my condition?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_4",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Yes — that's exactly what it's designed for. Zavelyn helps with opening/closing stiff fingers, reducing spasticity, improving grip and fine motor control, and rebuilding the brain–hand signal pathway.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_5",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Why is it better than alternatives?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_5",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Alternatives = passive tools. Zavelyn = active assisted therapy. Alternatives only strengthen muscles you can already use. Zavelyn rebuilds movement even when the hand is weak, stiff, or not responsive.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_6",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "What are your return policies?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_6",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>If you're not completely satisfied within the first 30 days, simply return it to us and we'll give you a full refund. You don't have to worry about returning it—we'll take care of that for you!</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_7",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Is it easy to use?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_7",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Very easy. Designed for seniors, stroke patients, and users with limited mobility. Large buttons, clear display, simple instructions. If you can press one button, you can use it.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_8",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "When will I see results?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_8",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Most users feel a difference within 1–3 weeks: reduced stiffness, improved finger mobility, and better control. Longer-term improvements typically appear after 4–8 weeks of daily use.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_9",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Do you include extras?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_9",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Yes. Every order includes: Free digital rehab guide, Free protection case, and Priority Support Access. Occasionally we add limited-time bonuses during promotions.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_10",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "What makes Zavelyn different?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_10",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Most devices rely on self-movement. Zavelyn assists the entire movement, trains each finger individually, uses structured rehab programs via display, supports neuro-muscular reactivation, and mimics clinic-grade equipment at home.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 11"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_11",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "Can I use Zavelyn if my hand cannot move at all?"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "a_11",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Yes. Even if your fingers cannot move voluntarily, the assisted motion can help maintain joint mobility and provide sensory feedback to the brain.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "FAQ 12"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_12",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "How do I get in touch?"
        },
